  "result": "The concept and its witnesses are written, but the gate never judged them. Both runs returned `SCOPE_VIOLATION` for a file I didn't write. Each shell command's output is saved under `.runtime/tmp/.../tasks/<id>.output`, which is inside the folder tree the gate watches for changes. So every gate run inside this session creates a new file there and fails for that reason alone. I can't prevent or delete those files, since the only command allowed is the gate itself. I stopped after 2 of the 6 runs, because more would have failed the same way. The harness's own re-run after the session should judge the files properly, as long as `.runtime/` is excluded or cleaned first.\n\n**The concept body** (`right_turn_through_region.lean`):\n- **Holds when:** at the observation where `a` stops overlapping `r` (`rises (¬ rel_occupies a r)`), its heading change since entering `r` is above −`u_turn_min` and at most −`turn_min`.\n- **Heading change:** `headingSince \"a\" step (rel_occupies a r)`, which integrates the yaw rate from the entry. The \"unknown\" cases come from it directly: entry not observed or overlap unknown since, a gap between observations longer than `step`, or a missing yaw rate.\n- **Holds once per passage:** because it only triggers at the exit, it can't hold again until `a` enters and leaves `r` again.\n- **Names used:** both claimed atoms, and only the formals and formal parameters. No literals, no narrowings.\n\n**The witnesses:**\n- **Setup:** `r` is a 20 m × 20 m roundabout; seven scenes, 1 s apart; `step` = 2 s, `turn_min` = 45°, `u_turn_min` = 135°.\n- **holds:** `a` enters at 2 s and exits at 5 s after turning right at −30°/s for three scenes, a −90° change.\n- **fails:** `a` passes straight through with no heading change.\n- **blind:** the holds trace with the yaw rate hidden.\n- **When each is judged:** only at the exit (`window := (5000, 5000)`). At every other observation the concept is false by definition, so checking the whole trace would turn `holds` into a violation.\n\nEarly on I also tried to search a Core file with `grep`. That was denied, so I read the files directly instead.\n\n`task_result.md` has the run log and these choices.",
